‪if you kept switching during the game?

676
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:30,378
‪Well, I thought it wasn't
‪the right thing to do.

677
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:33,089
‪I felt like I had to hurry
‪in that moment

678
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:35,258
‪and quickly make my mind up.

679
00:35:35,341 --> 00:35:36,884
‪You made your choice before the game.

680
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:37,802
‪No, I…

681
00:35:40,763 --> 00:35:42,807
‪-I didn't.
‪-I wanted to ask you this.

682
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:46,811
‪Was the moment you made your mind up

683
00:35:46,894 --> 00:35:48,813
‪after the secret date,

684
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:50,773
‪the moment you got back?

685
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:52,733
‪Ye-rim told me

686
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:55,653
‪that she saw you together.

687
00:35:55,736 --> 00:35:58,948
‪She said,
‪"Looks like we'll both leave here alone."

688
00:36:01,909 --> 00:36:03,703
‪He's saying her story doesn't add up.

689
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:04,704
‪You know that,

690
00:36:04,787 --> 00:36:07,748
‪when someone who's always smiley
‪suddenly gets serious,

691
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:08,958
‪-it's pretty scary.
‪-It's scary.

692
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,501
‪-It's really scary right now.
‪-Yeah.

693
00:36:11,085 --> 00:36:13,671
‪You already made your mind up.
‪Why blame it on the game?

694
00:36:13,754 --> 00:36:15,298
‪-No, I--
‪-As if you didn't know.

695
00:36:15,381 --> 00:36:16,549
‪-No, the thing is…
‪-Yeah?

696
00:36:17,258 --> 00:36:19,093
‪-Well--
‪-Be honest.

697
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:21,637
‪I'm being completely honest.

698
00:36:21,721 --> 00:36:25,641
‪At the time, I hadn't decided who to pick

699
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:27,560
‪as my final choice.

700
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:29,729
‪I just felt more swayed toward Kyung-ho.

701
00:36:30,354 --> 00:36:31,772
‪But then during the game,

702
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:34,525
‪I felt like I needed
‪to make my choice in that moment

703
00:36:35,109 --> 00:36:37,987
‪and make my feelings clear
‪toward just one person.

704
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:41,824
‪Or else you'd both be confused
‪or the situation would get weird.

705
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:48,164
‪And since I was leaning more
‪toward Kyung-ho…

706
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:51,459
‪-Good job.
‪-…that's what happened.

707
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:53,461
‪I get it.

708
00:36:57,506 --> 00:36:58,507
‪I wondered

709
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:04,388
‪if I could develop feelings for anyone
‪in such a short time.

710
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:06,057
‪-And you did.
‪-I ended up

711
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:08,976
‪-feeling a lot.
‪-Your feelings came, went, and changed.

712
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:11,145
‪-They turned hot and cold.
‪-But also,

713
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:14,023
‪it's been really hard.

714
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:17,360
‪I keep wondering
‪if I'm doing the right thing.

715
00:37:17,443 --> 00:37:19,278
‪I'm so confused.

716
00:37:21,614 --> 00:37:23,532
<i>‪I think I was a little aggressive.</i>

717
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:26,869
<i>‪And I think I clearly said</i>
<i>‪that I resented her.</i>

718
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:30,373
‪I asked her questions
‪I already knew the answer to.

719
00:37:30,456 --> 00:37:33,542
‪What's done was done
‪and there was no changing it.

720
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:38,506
‪I dragged it out for no reason
‪and got too emotional.

721
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:39,757
‪When I realized that,

722
00:37:40,549 --> 00:37:42,343
‪I put a stop to the conversation.

723
00:37:49,058 --> 00:37:50,851
‪I really liked you a lot.

724
00:37:51,852 --> 00:37:54,689
‪I didn't tell you this on the secret date,

725
00:37:54,772 --> 00:37:57,942
‪but I'm not in a stable place right now.

726
00:37:58,025 --> 00:38:00,403
‪Financially or with my job
‪as a diving instructor.

727
00:38:01,404 --> 00:38:02,822
‪So I was self-conscious about that.

728
00:38:04,323 --> 00:38:06,826
‪I knew you wanted someone secure…

729
00:38:06,909 --> 00:38:11,038
‪If we'd dated, I might not have been able
‪to give you what you wanted…

730
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:12,456
‪That's something I thought about.

731
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:17,295
‪Thanks for making me feel all this.

732
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:18,462
‪Oh, man.

733
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:20,756
‪I appreciate it.

734
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:25,928
‪My favorite memory is taking selfies
‪in our matching outfits.

735
00:38:27,179 --> 00:38:28,139
‪It's the same for me.

736
00:38:28,222 --> 00:38:30,224
‪-Yeah.
‪-So to be honest,

737
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:34,729
‪when I answered the question
‪about the most exciting moment,

738
00:38:35,354 --> 00:38:37,773
‪I don't think I was completely genuine.

739
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:39,859
‪I was going to question it but didn't.

740
00:38:39,942 --> 00:38:41,527
‪Because your mind seemed made up.

741
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:43,946
‪All right.

742
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:47,325
‪Well done.

743
00:38:48,743 --> 00:38:49,869
‪You're so popular.

744
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:52,621
‪I'm fine.

745
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:54,832
‪I'll get over this on my own.

746
00:38:56,417 --> 00:38:57,626
‪I feel a bit…

747
00:38:59,003 --> 00:39:01,422
‪I hope you don't get hurt this time.

748
00:39:05,217 --> 00:39:08,596
‪She said she's been hurt
‪by the guys she was drawn to.

749
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:09,764
‪She's doing it again,

750
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:11,891
‪-so he hopes she won't get hurt.
‪-By Kyung-ho.

751
00:39:11,974 --> 00:39:13,351
‪Wow, to the very end.

752
00:39:13,434 --> 00:39:15,311
‪How did they all develop
‪such deep feelings?

753
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:16,270
‪Right.

754
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:19,690
‪Usually, there are two guys and girls
‪who aren't interested in anyone

755
00:39:19,774 --> 00:39:21,317
‪-and just keep wandering.
‪-Right.

756
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,735
‪-There's always a wanderer.
‪-Totally.

757
00:39:22,818 --> 00:39:24,111
‪-Always!
‪-But not this time!

758
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:25,613
‪-They're all so sincere.
‪-Yeah.

759
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:28,240
‪From a viewer's perspective,
‪it's so much fun.

760
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:31,494
‪-I really appreciate it. Here's why.
‪-I'm so thankful.

761
00:39:31,577 --> 00:39:34,955
‪No joke, this moment has makes me
‪so proud of our show.

762
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:36,540
‪It's only been four days and--

763
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:39,251
‪-Tears, fighting, and drama.
‪-So much crying.

764
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:41,420
‪You'd think they've been dating
‪for months.

765
00:39:41,504 --> 00:39:42,880
‪Yeah. Gosh.

766
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:46,342
‪It's here.

767
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:54,141
‪The glamping tent will be open
‪to everyone until tomorrow morning.

768
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:58,604
<i>‪It says you can only use it</i>
<i>‪with one person of the opposite sex.</i>

769
00:39:58,687 --> 00:40:00,856
‪So I guess

770
00:40:01,524 --> 00:40:04,860
‪anyone who wants a bit more
‪lovey-dovey time can do so.

771
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:09,448
‪I think we can choose freely.

772
00:40:11,617 --> 00:40:13,202
‪Aren't you curious?

773
00:40:13,285 --> 00:40:14,829
‪-About what?
‪-Glamping.

774
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:15,913
‪Glamping?

775
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:20,876
‪Is it the last date?

776
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:22,503
‪-This? I think so.
‪-Yeah.

777
00:40:25,673 --> 00:40:26,674
‪Is everyone here?

778
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:28,426
‪-You're all here.
‪-Yeah.

779
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:34,432
‪You're drinking again?

780
00:40:42,189 --> 00:40:43,315
‪Aren't you drinking too much?

781
00:40:44,483 --> 00:40:45,401
‪It's our last night.

782
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:47,445
‪How much have you had?

783
00:40:49,155 --> 00:40:51,115
‪-I think about three bottles?
‪-Three bottles?

784
00:40:52,491 --> 00:40:53,868
‪-Stop drinking.
‪-Two or three.

785
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:56,328
‪Come on.

786
00:41:00,624 --> 00:41:02,418
‪I think you're drinking too much.

787
00:41:05,004 --> 00:41:06,797
‪It's fine. I'll stick close to Ha-yoon.

788
00:41:07,381 --> 00:41:09,800
‪-That's not the issue.
‪-Go have fun with Kyung-ho.

789
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:11,093
‪-What?
‪-Isn't he waiting for you?

790
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:12,428
‪No, he's not.

791
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:14,555
‪He might be.

792
00:41:14,638 --> 00:41:16,015
‪He's not.

793
00:41:16,098 --> 00:41:17,475
‪As we discussed,

794
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:21,604
‪I get it.

795
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:23,189
‪I got the message.

796
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:30,613
‪It's not that I didn't notice,
‪but I tried not to look.

797
00:41:30,696 --> 00:41:36,535
‪I felt like Ga-yeon and Jung-min
‪needed some closure,

798
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:38,871
<i>‪so I kept my distance.</i>

799
00:41:42,791 --> 00:41:44,168
‪You're here because you're sorry, right?

800
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:46,462
‪No. That's not why.

801
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:48,589
‪-Yes, it is.
‪-No, it's not.

802
00:41:49,089 --> 00:41:50,424
‪It's so obvious.

803
00:41:50,508 --> 00:41:51,592
‪That's not it.

804
00:41:53,344 --> 00:41:54,637
‪Then why are you here?

805
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:56,096
‪-Just.
‪-Just?

806
00:42:00,351 --> 00:42:02,937
‪Ye-rim is so strong-minded.

807
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:05,189
‪Why?

808
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:07,066
‪-Because she's not bothered?
‪-What?

809
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:10,778
‪Because she's handling
‪the situation so well?

810
00:42:11,362 --> 00:42:13,948
‪Yeah, she's in a similar situation to me.

811
00:42:14,698 --> 00:42:17,576
‪Of course, she was in this position first.

812
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:20,329
‪-Which is better?
‪-What do you mean?

813
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:24,333
‪Finding out your feelings
‪are one-sided before the final vote

814
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:26,293
‪or finding out after the first day?

815
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:28,379
‪I'd rather find out at the end
‪and be blindsided.

816
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:30,714
‪-Me too. I'd rather find out at the end.
‪-Right?

817
00:42:30,798 --> 00:42:33,092
‪I couldn't handle
‪being in Ye-rim's position.

818
00:42:33,175 --> 00:42:34,760
‪I couldn't endure several days of that.

819
00:42:34,843 --> 00:42:36,804
‪I'd rather have fun
‪and suffer a bit at the end,

820
00:42:36,887 --> 00:42:38,097
‪have a drink, and forget.

821
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:41,058
‪-Say goodbye, call a taxi, and go home.
‪-Exactly.

822
00:42:41,642 --> 00:42:44,311
‪Yeah, she's in a similar situation to me.

823
00:42:44,979 --> 00:42:47,731
‪Of course, she was in this position first.

824
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:50,192
‪I'm just going through it now.

825
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:01,245
‪I think I felt a bit uncomfortable

826
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:03,581
‪by his changed attitude.

827
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:08,460
‪I obviously didn't expect him
‪to be nice to me after I hurt him.

828
00:43:10,296 --> 00:43:12,339
<i>‪But he was acting so differently</i>

829
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:15,426
<i>‪that it was hard to be around him.</i>

830
00:43:20,723 --> 00:43:21,724
‪This is so frustrating.

831
00:43:23,934 --> 00:43:25,102
‪Me too.

832
00:43:27,396 --> 00:43:29,023
‪Ga-yeon, I…

833
00:43:29,648 --> 00:43:31,567
‪-What's wrong?
‪-Why's Jung-min acting like that?

834
00:43:31,650 --> 00:43:32,526
‪Like what?

835
00:43:36,155 --> 00:43:37,448
‪-Jung-min.
‪-Yeah?

836
00:43:39,158 --> 00:43:41,702
‪I don't know. It's tough.

837
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:43,495
‪Did I tease her too much?

838
00:43:44,496 --> 00:43:46,206
‪Maybe I did.

839
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:50,836
‪Hey, Kyung-ho.

840
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,006
‪I think I was a bit too harsh.

841
00:43:55,341 --> 00:43:56,342
‪You should talk to her.

842
00:43:59,011 --> 00:43:59,970
‪I'm sorry.

843
00:44:00,054 --> 00:44:00,888
‪Not at all.

844
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:02,973
‪He's leaving it to Kyung-ho.

845
00:44:03,057 --> 00:44:05,684
‪What's wrong with you? What are you doing?

846
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:10,356
‪Shouldn't I give her some time alone?

847
00:44:16,528 --> 00:44:17,780
‪And also…

848
00:44:19,114 --> 00:44:21,367
‪I don't know what this is,

849
00:44:23,285 --> 00:44:25,954
‪-but during the game,
‪-Yeah?

850
00:44:26,038 --> 00:44:29,958
‪remember I held both their hands?

851
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:35,673
‪But I think my heart raced more
‪when Jung-min held my hand…

852
00:44:37,132 --> 00:44:38,175
‪I want to come in.

853
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:40,469
‪Should I leave?

854
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:42,513
‪No, it's fine.

855
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:44,765
‪Sit over there.

856
00:44:44,848 --> 00:44:46,558
‪Can I sit here?

857
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:52,439
‪Seriously.

858
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:56,693
‪Did you not see what just happened?

859
00:44:56,777 --> 00:44:58,278
‪You didn't see, did you?

860
00:44:58,362 --> 00:44:59,863
‪I tried not to look on purpose.

861
00:45:01,073 --> 00:45:03,700
‪He kept saying, "Go to Kyung-ho."

862
00:45:03,784 --> 00:45:07,246
‪"Go and have fun with him.
‪He's waiting for you."

863
00:45:07,329 --> 00:45:08,747
‪He kept making it

864
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:11,166
‪really uncomfortable.

865
00:45:12,084 --> 00:45:13,210
‪I mean,

866
00:45:14,420 --> 00:45:15,754
‪why can't he accept it?

867
00:45:17,047 --> 00:45:19,842
‪From his perspective,

868
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:22,719
‪it's obviously disappointing.

869
00:45:22,803 --> 00:45:24,471
‪He told me this.

870
00:45:25,639 --> 00:45:28,892
‪Ye-rim found out yesterday…

871
00:45:28,976 --> 00:45:32,896
‪but he only just found out.

872
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:38,026
‪But the way he's expressing his anger…

873
00:45:38,902 --> 00:45:41,655
‪I don't know if it's the alcohol talking,

874
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:45,993
‪but I feel like he's crossing a line.

875
00:45:48,120 --> 00:45:52,875
‪I get how you feel…

876
00:45:53,709 --> 00:45:55,586
‪but Ga-yeon

877
00:45:56,420 --> 00:46:00,007
‪you should just accept
‪how he's acting too.

878
00:46:00,090 --> 00:46:02,801
‪What can you do? That's how he feels.

879
00:46:02,885 --> 00:46:06,430
‪You can't control his emotions.

880
00:46:07,681 --> 00:46:11,351
‪Jung-min has a right to be angry
‪about the choice you made.

881
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:15,898
‪If you push him to get over it,

882
00:46:15,981 --> 00:46:17,524
‪that's selfish.

883
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:25,532
‪Bravo!

884
00:46:26,074 --> 00:46:27,701
‪-Hye-won!
‪-Hye-won!

885
00:46:27,784 --> 00:46:29,203
‪-Hye-won!
‪-Hye-won!

886
00:46:29,286 --> 00:46:31,163
‪The queen is right!

887
00:46:31,246 --> 00:46:32,915
‪The queen is different!

888
00:46:32,998 --> 00:46:33,957
‪This is crazy.

889
00:46:34,041 --> 00:46:35,834
‪-So good.
‪-She's doing our job for us.

890
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:37,961
‪So this is why people
‪watch reaction videos.

891
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:40,839
‪-How did she say exactly what I wanted?
‪-She's so wise and insightful.

892
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:44,676
‪-You're right.
‪-Yeah.

893
00:46:45,677 --> 00:46:48,180
‪I think he's still drinking too much.

894
00:46:48,263 --> 00:46:49,765
‪Just let him.

895
00:46:49,848 --> 00:46:51,850
‪That's what he wants to do.

896
00:46:52,351 --> 00:46:54,394
‪Stop trying to solve things.

897
00:46:57,064 --> 00:46:59,358
‪-He'll be fine when he sobers up, right?
‪-Huh?

898
00:46:59,441 --> 00:47:01,568
‪-He's just drunk, right?
‪-Of course.

899
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:03,278
‪Yeah. This isn't him.

900
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:05,989
‪-Right, he's not…
‪-He's not the Jung-min I know.

901
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:20,629
‪Ye-rim, you're really strong.

902
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:24,466
‪-Seriously.
‪-Did something happen?

903
00:47:26,552 --> 00:47:27,386
‪I think I was

904
00:47:28,345 --> 00:47:29,972
‪-a bit too harsh on her.
‪-Really?

905
00:47:31,014 --> 00:47:32,099
‪That you were disappointed?

906
00:47:32,975 --> 00:47:35,686
‪Yeah, that kind of thing.
‪I feel a bit bad,

907
00:47:35,769 --> 00:47:36,979
‪seeing how she was just now.

908
00:47:38,939 --> 00:47:41,149
‪I just blurted things out
‪without meaning to.

909
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:42,651
‪I suddenly feel really bad.

910
00:47:44,152 --> 00:47:46,488
‪Now that I'm in your position…

911
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:49,241
‪-I felt that way yesterday.
‪-Yeah.

912
00:47:50,200 --> 00:47:51,493
‪It is annoying, though.

913
00:47:52,661 --> 00:47:53,620
‪Kyung-ho

914
00:47:55,038 --> 00:47:56,415
‪went to you,

915
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:01,628
‪then he slid over to Ga-yeon.

916
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:03,589
‪He opened up to both of you.

917
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:04,506
‪Yeah.

918
00:48:04,590 --> 00:48:07,301
‪This is really irritating.

919
00:48:09,636 --> 00:48:10,470
‪What can I do?

920
00:48:11,763 --> 00:48:12,931
‪You liked him,

921
00:48:14,474 --> 00:48:17,102
‪and Ga-yeon liked him.

922
00:48:17,978 --> 00:48:19,521
‪And I was on the sideline.

923
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:21,982
‪And you were by Kyung-ho's side.

924
00:48:22,065 --> 00:48:23,150
‪Odd one out, odd one out.

925
00:48:25,068 --> 00:48:26,486
‪This is really irritating.

926
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:29,865
‪I thought I had pretty high self-esteem.

927
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:30,782
‪Yeah.

928
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:33,869
‪It's even more irritating
‪because of Kyung-ho.

929
00:48:33,952 --> 00:48:35,495
‪I feel petty for no good reason.

930
00:48:35,579 --> 00:48:36,580
‪I felt the same way.

931
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:39,041
‪I resented Ga-yeon too.

932
00:48:44,379 --> 00:48:45,505
‪But…

933
00:48:46,173 --> 00:48:49,843
‪Jung-min may have felt confident,

934
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:53,972
‪but that was on him, right?
‪Did you give him reason to feel that?

935
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:59,394
‪When he said he was sure about us,
‪I didn't deny it.

936
00:49:00,103 --> 00:49:03,982
‪So he might have felt
‪I was returning his feelings.

937
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:05,484
‪That's probably how he felt.

938
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:08,528
<i>‪He probably felt quite secure,</i>

939
00:49:08,612 --> 00:49:11,490
<i>‪-and that turned into certainty.</i>
<i>‪-You're right.</i>

940
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:16,244
‪But I don't think
‪you should beat yourself…

941
00:49:16,328 --> 00:49:18,288
‪-No, you don't.
‪-Not at all.

942
00:49:18,372 --> 00:49:19,289
‪One, two, three.

943
00:49:19,373 --> 00:49:21,792
‪-You don't need to beat yourself up.
‪-Don't beat yourself up.

944
00:49:25,837 --> 00:49:29,508
‪-I just…
‪-The one thing I want to say to you is

945
00:49:30,092 --> 00:49:33,220
‪that it's not like you didn't do enough
‪or did anything wrong.

946
00:49:33,303 --> 00:49:36,181
‪-Yeah. I know that for sure.
‪-Yeah. You know that, right?

947
00:49:37,015 --> 00:49:39,643
‪But at least Ga-yeon

948
00:49:39,726 --> 00:49:43,939
‪went to talk to you
‪as soon as we got back.

949
00:49:44,022 --> 00:49:46,817
‪I think she deserves credit for that,
‪unlike someone else.

950
00:49:51,196 --> 00:49:53,657
‪Where are they? Are they in the tent?

951
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:54,574
‪Her and Kyung-ho?

952
00:49:55,283 --> 00:49:57,244
‪Should I go check?

953
00:50:04,543 --> 00:50:05,961
‪Did you want to go to bed, Ye-rim?

954
00:50:07,587 --> 00:50:09,589
‪Where did Chae-rin go?

955
00:50:10,465 --> 00:50:11,591
‪-Her and Do-geon.
‪-Do-geon?

956
00:50:11,675 --> 00:50:13,135
‪-Maybe the tent?
‪-The tent?

957
00:50:15,095 --> 00:50:16,596
‪CHAE-RIN AND DO-GEON
‪DISCUSS THEIR IDEAL TYPES

958
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:19,015
‪Whoever I'm into is my type.

959
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:21,893
‪I don't really have a specific ideal type.

960
00:50:23,520 --> 00:50:25,397
‪-But one thing is for sure.
‪-What?

961
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:26,314
‪Personality.

962
00:50:26,940 --> 00:50:30,068
‪-Oh, someone who's outgoing and chatty?
‪-If our personalities don't match,

963
00:50:30,152 --> 00:50:33,405
‪I can't date them,
‪even if they are physically my type.

964
00:50:33,488 --> 00:50:35,907
‪In terms of faces,
‪they just need to be pretty.

965
00:50:38,285 --> 00:50:39,286
‪You're pretty.

966
00:50:39,911 --> 00:50:41,163
‪-Me?
‪-Yeah.

967
00:50:42,038 --> 00:50:42,998
‪Of course, I am.

968
00:50:46,334 --> 00:50:48,295
‪Do I fit your ideal type?

969
00:50:49,671 --> 00:50:50,505
‪For me,

970
00:50:51,214 --> 00:50:52,924
‪I like an edge-of-tofu face.

971
00:50:53,008 --> 00:50:53,884
‪"Edge-of-tofu."

972
00:50:57,846 --> 00:51:02,100
‪Why does everyone on this show
‪like edge-of-tofu faces so much?

973
00:51:02,934 --> 00:51:04,060
‪I'm scared.

974
00:51:04,770 --> 00:51:06,521
‪Was it Ji-young who liked
‪an edge-of-tofu face?

975
00:51:07,564 --> 00:51:08,440
‪Scary.

976
00:51:09,858 --> 00:51:10,901
‪That actually works?

977
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:13,320
‪I like an edge-of-tofu face.

978
00:51:13,403 --> 00:51:14,738
‪"Edge-of-tofu."

979
00:51:14,821 --> 00:51:16,698
‪What is an edge-of-tofu face?

980
00:51:17,282 --> 00:51:18,116
‪Come in.

981
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:21,203
‪-Can I come in?
‪-Yeah.

982
00:51:21,286 --> 00:51:24,080
‪Do you know what an edge-of-tofu type is?

983
00:51:24,164 --> 00:51:25,832
‪-What?
‪-An edge-of-tofu type.

984
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:27,375
‪-Edge-of-tofu type?
‪-Yeah.

985
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:29,294
‪Isn't that you?

986
00:51:31,213 --> 00:51:37,010
‪It's when you have an angular look
‪like the edges of a tofu block.

987
00:51:37,093 --> 00:51:38,887
‪Spot on. A SNU graduate, indeed.

988
00:51:38,970 --> 00:51:41,181
‪Anyway, it's you, right?

989
00:51:41,264 --> 00:51:42,224
‪She means you, right?

990
00:51:42,307 --> 00:51:43,517
‪-I guess so.
‪-Yeah. Okay.

991
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:44,851
‪Have a nice chat.

992
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:46,394
‪Impressive.

993
00:51:47,687 --> 00:51:48,939
‪Who is that guy?

994
00:51:49,022 --> 00:51:51,650
‪-I love Ha-yoon.
‪-He's great.

995
00:51:52,734 --> 00:51:54,069
‪When you all walked in one by one,

996
00:51:54,861 --> 00:51:56,488
‪you came in last, right?

997
00:51:57,823 --> 00:52:00,617
‪But they were a bit intense
‪and a bit too much.

998
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:02,953
‪I couldn't figure out the last one…

999
00:52:03,620 --> 00:52:04,913
‪Then I saw your edge-of-tofu face.

1000
00:52:05,872 --> 00:52:07,374
‪I was like, "Is this destiny?"

1001
00:52:08,917 --> 00:52:09,835
‪"This is the guy."

1002
00:52:11,628 --> 00:52:13,463
‪But honestly,

1003
00:52:13,547 --> 00:52:18,385
‪I wasn't sure if I'd fall for anyone
‪on this show.

1004
00:52:18,468 --> 00:52:20,345
‪-Totally.
‪-Yeah.

1005
00:52:20,428 --> 00:52:23,390
‪-I was skeptical.
‪-Same.

1006
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:27,185
‪But then I came here and met you.

1007
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:32,274
‪I mean, what?

1008
00:52:32,899 --> 00:52:33,775
‪Come again?

1009
00:52:33,859 --> 00:52:36,236
‪I like him more as time goes on.

1010
00:52:48,248 --> 00:52:51,418
‪Ha-yoon and Hye-won split up
‪to counsel different people.

1011
00:52:51,501 --> 00:52:52,752
‪They'll reunite in the tent later.

1012
00:52:52,836 --> 00:52:55,922
‪-"Honey, how did it go with you?"
‪-You're right.

1013
00:52:56,006 --> 00:52:57,841
‪"This is the story I heard."

1014
00:52:57,924 --> 00:53:00,760
‪"The kids under my care
‪are really angry right now."

1015
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:02,721
‪"I get where they're coming from."

1016
00:53:02,804 --> 00:53:05,015
‪-"Here's what I think."
‪-They're such a secure couple.

1017
00:53:05,640 --> 00:53:07,684
‪I can hear everything.
‪I hear Kyung-ho's voice

1018
00:53:08,810 --> 00:53:10,020
‪and Ga-yeon's voice.

1019
00:53:10,979 --> 00:53:13,315
‪Does it make you uncomfortable?

1020
00:53:13,398 --> 00:53:14,399
‪It freaking sucks.

1021
00:53:18,695 --> 00:53:20,488
‪You understand how I feel, right?

1022
00:53:21,072 --> 00:53:22,866
‪I do understand, honestly.

1023
00:53:23,867 --> 00:53:25,160
‪The situation sucks.

1024
00:53:29,497 --> 00:53:30,707
‪I'm drunk.

1025
00:53:35,587 --> 00:53:37,297
‪Did they enjoy the tent?

1026
00:53:38,673 --> 00:53:40,800
<i>‪-Do-geon and--</i>
<i>‪-Did they go?</i>

1027
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:42,469
<i>‪Weren't they in the tent</i>

1028
00:53:42,552 --> 00:53:44,304
<i>‪when Ye-rim came looking for them?</i>

1029
00:53:44,387 --> 00:53:45,472
‪NO ONE'S USED IT YET

1030
00:53:45,555 --> 00:53:46,806
‪Should we go?

1031
00:53:46,890 --> 00:53:47,933
‪Do you want to?

1032
00:53:48,016 --> 00:53:49,100
‪Go on.

1033
00:53:51,519 --> 00:53:53,188
‪-See you later.
‪-Okay.

1034
00:53:54,314 --> 00:53:56,191
‪Have fun.

1035
00:53:56,274 --> 00:54:00,111
<i>‪I wanted the two of us to have a chat,</i>

1036
00:54:00,195 --> 00:54:01,404
<i>‪being the last night and all.</i>

1037
00:54:01,488 --> 00:54:02,822
‪I'm so annoyed.

1038
00:54:02,906 --> 00:54:03,907
‪Let's have one final drink.

1039
00:54:04,741 --> 00:54:07,911
<i>‪So we made use of the tent.</i>

1040
00:54:11,665 --> 00:54:13,416
‪-Inside?
‪-No.

1041
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:14,542
‪Chairs?

1042
00:54:17,754 --> 00:54:19,589
‪-Is it warm?
‪-No.

1043
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:21,174
‪-Oh, it is warm.
‪-It's warm.

1044
00:54:21,257 --> 00:54:22,384
‪Let's zip this up.

1045
00:54:23,635 --> 00:54:24,928
‪How did you know to do that?

1046
00:54:25,011 --> 00:54:26,554
‪-I was here before.
‪-Oh, right.

1047
00:54:36,856 --> 00:54:38,817
‪Gosh, how is it so warm?

1048
00:54:38,900 --> 00:54:40,443
‪-It's warm.
‪-Yeah, it's nice.

1049
00:54:50,829 --> 00:54:52,664
‪-It's all over.
‪-Tell me about it.

1050
00:54:54,124 --> 00:54:56,710
‪I wished we had more time
‪up until yesterday.

1051
00:54:57,711 --> 00:54:59,379
‪I don't feel like that at all now.

1052
00:55:01,423 --> 00:55:02,382
‪This is enough.

1053
00:55:03,216 --> 00:55:04,551
‪Your hands are so big.

1054
00:55:05,719 --> 00:55:07,220
‪Maybe your hands are small.

1055
00:55:07,303 --> 00:55:08,888
‪I do have really small hands.

1056
00:55:08,972 --> 00:55:10,140
‪That could be why.

1057
00:55:11,224 --> 00:55:12,976
‪For the last five days…

1058
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:16,646
‪"Long five days?"

1059
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:18,231
‪-Last five days.
‪-Oh, last five days…

1060
00:55:18,314 --> 00:55:21,568
‪I'm really thankful.

1061
00:55:21,651 --> 00:55:22,610
‪Me too.

1062
00:55:25,447 --> 00:55:28,116
‪We need to sleep. Oh, that's right.
‪How should we do this?

1063
00:55:28,199 --> 00:55:29,075
‪There's three of us.

1064
00:55:30,618 --> 00:55:32,287
‪Did Ga-yeon go to the tent?

1065
00:55:32,370 --> 00:55:33,621
‪Won't the two sleep there?

1066
00:56:04,444 --> 00:56:05,487
‪Are you going to bed?

1067
00:56:06,821 --> 00:56:08,656
‪They're in the tent.

1068
00:56:10,825 --> 00:56:12,285
‪You can hear everything.

1069
00:56:12,368 --> 00:56:13,328
‪What?

1070
00:56:13,411 --> 00:56:14,579
‪Just go to bed.

1071
00:56:23,463 --> 00:56:27,175
‪CHAE-RIN AND DO-GEON COME OUTSIDE

1072
00:56:32,680 --> 00:56:36,851
‪THE TENT IS ALREADY ZIPPED UP

1073
00:56:36,935 --> 00:56:38,853
‪They closed the flap.

1074
00:56:39,521 --> 00:56:41,147
‪So that's how you close it.

1075
00:56:41,981 --> 00:56:43,691
‪It's zipped up?

1076
00:56:44,317 --> 00:56:45,318
‪Unbelievable.

1077
00:56:47,403 --> 00:56:49,572
‪Did Ga-yeon and Kyung-ho go out?

1078
00:56:49,656 --> 00:56:50,698
‪Yeah.

1079
00:56:50,782 --> 00:56:51,825
‪-To the tent?
‪-For real?

1080
00:56:52,408 --> 00:56:53,284
‪Yeah.

1081
00:56:53,368 --> 00:56:55,453
‪What about that poor guy?

1082
00:56:59,249 --> 00:57:00,959
‪It was Jung-min who told me.

1083
00:57:01,042 --> 00:57:02,585
‪-What?
‪-Jung-min told me.

1084
00:57:04,546 --> 00:57:06,673
‪-See? We should have taken it first.
‪-Right.

1085
00:57:06,756 --> 00:57:08,716
‪Poor Jung-min.

1086
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:10,969
‪-Maybe we really should have left earlier.
‪-Right.

1087
00:57:11,052 --> 00:57:12,720
‪Why did they go to the tent?

1088
00:57:14,180 --> 00:57:15,140
‪Hurry and go to bed.

1089
00:57:15,807 --> 00:57:17,142
‪-You hurry.
‪-Okay.

1090
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:20,186
‪Let's just sleep in here together.

1091
00:57:20,270 --> 00:57:21,855
‪No.

1092
00:57:22,480 --> 00:57:23,565
‪Go to bed.

1093
00:57:24,232 --> 00:57:25,108
‪See you tomorrow.

1094
00:57:28,236 --> 00:57:30,780
‪-Isn't it all sorted out now?
‪-Yeah.

1095
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:32,323
‪Jung-min too.

1096
00:57:32,949 --> 00:57:34,159
‪You think it's sorted?

1097
00:57:34,242 --> 00:57:35,660
‪I'm asking if it's sorted.

1098
00:57:36,369 --> 00:57:37,412
‪Right now?

1099
00:57:37,495 --> 00:57:38,455
‪Yeah.

1100
00:57:38,538 --> 00:57:39,414
‪My feelings?

1101
00:57:40,165 --> 00:57:41,958
‪Didn't you talk everything out?

1102
00:57:42,041 --> 00:57:43,918
‪-Yeah, we did.
‪-Then…

1103
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:45,128
‪I said everything I wanted.

1104
00:57:45,211 --> 00:57:47,964
‪So there's nothing more you can do, right?

1105
00:57:48,548 --> 00:57:52,135
‪-Really?
‪-I handled it well.

1106
00:57:52,218 --> 00:57:53,553
‪-How?
‪-Just…

1107
00:57:54,762 --> 00:57:56,139
‪-You were smart about it?
‪-Yeah.

1108
00:57:57,474 --> 00:57:59,517
‪-All in the palm of your hand.
‪-Yeah.

1109
00:58:00,101 --> 00:58:01,853
‪It went exactly as I expected.

1110
00:58:03,104 --> 00:58:04,856
‪I talked about this with Do-geon,

1111
00:58:04,939 --> 00:58:05,815
‪but it was over

1112
00:58:07,442 --> 00:58:08,735
‪when she touched my eye.

1113
00:58:09,444 --> 00:58:10,945
‪-Huh?
‪-When she touched my eye,

1114
00:58:11,613 --> 00:58:12,572
‪that ended it.

1115
00:58:12,655 --> 00:58:13,698
‪What do you mean?

1116
00:58:14,782 --> 00:58:15,617
‪Here.

1117
00:58:16,326 --> 00:58:18,995
<i>‪I don't remember who made the first move,</i>

1118
00:58:19,078 --> 00:58:20,914
<i>‪but we ended up holding hands.</i>

1119
00:58:25,001 --> 00:58:27,170
‪But rather than holding hands like this,

1120
00:58:27,253 --> 00:58:29,047
‪holding it like this
‪makes my heart race more.

1121
00:58:29,130 --> 00:58:30,381
‪All ticklish.

1122
00:58:31,007 --> 00:58:31,966
‪I did, but…

1123
00:58:32,592 --> 00:58:35,637
<i>‪I had butterflies</i>
<i>‪around Ga-yeon the whole time.</i>

1124
00:58:37,180 --> 00:58:38,264
<i>‪My heart fluttered.</i>

1125
00:58:41,100 --> 00:58:42,769
‪I didn't know.

1126
00:58:42,852 --> 00:58:46,105
‪I thought I was being really smart,

1127
00:58:46,189 --> 00:58:48,525
‪but nothing worked out the way I wanted.

1128
00:58:48,608 --> 00:58:50,109
‪Everything went my way.

1129
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:52,612
‪Impressive. You're amazing.

1130
00:58:52,695 --> 00:58:54,072
‪-I am, aren't I?
‪-Yeah.

1131
00:59:03,331 --> 00:59:06,084
‪It didn't feel like this
‪when I came here with Do-geon.

1132
00:59:07,210 --> 00:59:08,920
‪When you came here with Do-geon?

1133
00:59:09,003 --> 00:59:10,922
‪I really hated that tent.

1134
00:59:11,673 --> 00:59:15,009
<i>‪Do-geon and I laid down</i>
<i>‪as far apart as possible.</i>

1135
00:59:15,593 --> 00:59:17,554
<i>‪But Kyung-ho and I were</i>
<i>‪really close together.</i>

1136
00:59:17,637 --> 00:59:20,848
<i>‪We weren't right up against each other,</i>
<i>‪but we only left a small gap.</i>

1137
00:59:20,932 --> 00:59:23,393
‪I told Kyung-ho

1138
00:59:23,476 --> 00:59:25,895
‪that I don't get physical with guys
‪unless I'm dating them.

1139
00:59:29,274 --> 00:59:30,567
‪We're touching now.

1140
00:59:32,026 --> 00:59:33,695
‪Points deducted.

1141
00:59:33,778 --> 00:59:34,779
‪Right.

1142
00:59:35,363 --> 00:59:36,698
<i>‪I think it's important</i>

1143
00:59:36,781 --> 00:59:39,909
<i>‪when it comes to things</i>
<i>‪like physical touch.</i>

1144
00:59:39,993 --> 00:59:44,038
<i>‪Because it can actually</i>
<i>‪make you grow closer.</i>

1145
00:59:44,581 --> 00:59:45,623
‪What are you going to do?

1146
00:59:47,917 --> 00:59:48,918
‪I'm still going to hold it.

1147
00:59:50,878 --> 00:59:51,921
‪Okay.

1148
00:59:54,424 --> 00:59:58,803
‪I try to be pretty disciplined,

1149
00:59:58,886 --> 01:00:02,181
‪but that's not so easy
‪when it comes to love.

1150
01:00:03,641 --> 01:00:06,603
‪I really want to be
‪a self-controlled person.

1151
01:00:06,686 --> 01:00:07,520
‪Yeah?

1152
01:00:08,229 --> 01:00:09,063
‪But

1153
01:00:09,856 --> 01:00:10,857
‪I'm failing.

1154
01:00:13,192 --> 01:00:16,613
<i>‪I tend to lose my head a little</i>
<i>‪in that kind of setting.</i>

1155
01:00:17,196 --> 01:00:19,782
<i>‪With that kind of scent</i>

1156
01:00:20,867 --> 01:00:21,826
<i>‪and atmosphere.</i>

1157
01:00:25,121 --> 01:00:26,205
‪I can't control myself.

1158
01:00:29,375 --> 01:00:30,835
‪It would be weird if you could.

1159
01:00:30,918 --> 01:00:32,962
‪It's impossible.

1160
01:00:34,756 --> 01:00:36,049
‪I thought I'd be able to.

1161
01:00:38,468 --> 01:00:42,305
‪How many times did you say
‪your head hurt over the last two days?

1162
01:00:43,306 --> 01:00:44,390
‪About 40 times?

1163
01:00:44,474 --> 01:00:45,975
‪I think it was about 100 times.

1164
01:00:46,059 --> 01:00:46,893
‪Really?

1165
01:00:47,518 --> 01:00:50,104
‪-No, you probably said it about 40 times.
‪-Yeah, 40.

1166
01:01:13,878 --> 01:01:15,129
‪How should we sleep?

1167
01:01:15,213 --> 01:01:17,882
‪I feel like she might not sleep out there.

1168
01:01:17,965 --> 01:01:19,759
‪They'll definitely sleep outside tonight.

1169
01:01:19,842 --> 01:01:21,511
‪-You think?
‪-Probably.

1170
01:01:22,011 --> 01:01:23,137
‪I don't think so. Let's check.

1171
01:01:24,347 --> 01:01:26,265
‪They already closed the tent.

1172
01:01:26,349 --> 01:01:28,351
‪-You're right.
‪-It's zipped up already.

1173
01:01:28,935 --> 01:01:30,812
‪-That's insane.
‪-I saw it.

1174
01:01:38,695 --> 01:01:40,446
‪They're giggling and flirting
‪inside the tent.

1175
01:01:41,447 --> 01:01:42,949
‪You can hear them so clearly,

1176
01:01:45,410 --> 01:01:47,954
‪being all lovey-dovey.

1177
01:01:50,123 --> 01:01:52,333
‪It's harder because
‪I didn't see it coming.

1178
01:01:55,044 --> 01:01:57,171
‪The fact that we're talking about this
‪means we need to get up.

1179
01:01:57,255 --> 01:01:58,464
‪Okay.

1180
01:02:01,968 --> 01:02:04,637
‪I said I wouldn't even
‪consider a younger guy.

1181
01:02:09,934 --> 01:02:12,603
‪Things don't always go the way you plan.

1182
01:02:13,479 --> 01:02:14,313
‪Yeah.

1183
01:02:15,440 --> 01:02:17,233
‪-You try.
‪-What?

1184
01:02:17,984 --> 01:02:19,110
‪Write something.

1185
01:02:27,243 --> 01:02:29,662
<i>‪She wrote a message on my palm.</i>

1186
01:02:31,164 --> 01:02:31,998
‪Jung?

1187
01:02:34,542 --> 01:02:35,543
‪What is it?

1188
01:02:39,088 --> 01:02:40,590
‪It felt like she wrote, "I like you."

1189
01:02:41,382 --> 01:02:44,177
‪So I said I wanted to try it too.

1190
01:02:44,260 --> 01:02:45,636
‪-Now, I'll try.
‪-Okay.

1191
01:02:45,720 --> 01:02:47,054
‪-This is the bottom.
‪-Okay.

1192
01:02:49,891 --> 01:02:51,225
<i>‪I wrote, "Me too."</i>

1193
01:02:57,023 --> 01:02:58,900
‪You could do it with me.
‪Don't you want to?

1194
01:02:58,983 --> 01:02:59,817
‪I do.

1195
01:03:12,997 --> 01:03:14,207
‪So refreshing.

1196
01:03:29,305 --> 01:03:31,015
‪-I hear them so well.
‪-I know.

1197
01:03:31,808 --> 01:03:33,184
‪What?

1198
01:03:34,060 --> 01:03:36,521
‪-Oh, Hye-won.
‪-Sorry.

1199
01:03:36,604 --> 01:03:37,814
‪What is it?

1200
01:03:37,897 --> 01:03:39,023
‪The noise.

1201
01:03:39,106 --> 01:03:40,358
‪What noise?

1202
01:03:41,108 --> 01:03:43,820
‪-Oh, them talking?
‪-Yeah.

1203
01:03:43,903 --> 01:03:46,739
‪-You can't hear what they're saying.
‪-You can't make out what it is.

1204
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:50,576
‪-You're really busy, right?
‪-What?

1205
01:03:51,160 --> 01:03:52,411
‪-With work.
‪-Work?

1206
01:03:53,579 --> 01:03:56,833
‪What's your schedule like back home?

1207
01:03:58,084 --> 01:04:01,921
‪It does get a bit busy
‪but I'll have plenty of time to meet up.

1208
01:04:02,004 --> 01:04:02,922
‪Really?

1209
01:04:03,005 --> 01:04:03,840
‪Yeah.

1210
01:04:04,757 --> 01:04:05,633
‪You're busy, right?

1211
01:04:05,716 --> 01:04:06,592
‪-Me?
‪-Yeah.

1212
01:04:06,676 --> 01:04:08,761
‪My schedule is super flexible.

1213
01:04:08,845 --> 01:04:10,471
‪As long as I get my work done.

1214
01:04:12,056 --> 01:04:13,683
‪-Performance-based?
‪-Yeah.

1215
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:14,600
‪I'm someone

1216
01:04:15,434 --> 01:04:19,355
‪who needs to win no matter what
‪when it comes to work.

1217
01:04:20,731 --> 01:04:22,066
‪Did you win in here?

1218
01:04:22,149 --> 01:04:24,569
‪I lost. No, I won.

1219
01:04:24,652 --> 01:04:25,528
‪-What?
‪-No.

1220
01:04:26,487 --> 01:04:28,656
‪Did you happily lose?

1221
01:04:28,739 --> 01:04:30,825
‪There were a few unexpected twists,

1222
01:04:31,993 --> 01:04:32,869
‪but

1223
01:04:33,744 --> 01:04:35,705
‪it worked out the way I wanted.

1224
01:04:36,956 --> 01:04:38,249
‪I think it's getting brighter.

1225
01:04:38,332 --> 01:04:39,375
‪The sun must be rising.

1226
01:04:39,458 --> 01:04:40,501
‪What time is it?

1227
01:04:44,881 --> 01:04:45,840
‪You're falling asleep.

1228
01:04:45,923 --> 01:04:47,341
‪-I'm sleepy.
‪-Me too.

1229
01:04:48,593 --> 01:04:49,886
‪Should we sleep?

1230
01:04:49,969 --> 01:04:52,138
‪We should wash up.
‪We'll need to shower later anyway.

1231
01:04:52,221 --> 01:04:53,180
‪I know.

1232
01:04:53,264 --> 01:04:54,974
‪Let's get up for real now.

1233
01:04:55,057 --> 01:04:56,976
‪-We really have to get up.
‪-I can't be bothered.

1234
01:04:57,059 --> 01:04:59,228
‪I know, but we still need to get up.

1235
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:00,313
‪I'm so…

1236
01:05:05,985 --> 01:05:07,737
‪I'll come back at 8 o'clock.

1237
01:05:07,820 --> 01:05:09,655
‪-Okay.
‪-Good night.

1238
01:05:09,739 --> 01:05:10,573
‪Okay.

1239
01:05:15,661 --> 01:05:17,538
‪-Just sleep here.
‪-What?

1240
01:05:18,122 --> 01:05:19,665
‪No, I can't.

1241
01:05:19,749 --> 01:05:20,875
‪I need to wash up.

1242
01:05:25,296 --> 01:05:26,797
‪I need to wash up.

1243
01:05:26,881 --> 01:05:29,634
‪-Come on. I worked hard to get up.
‪-Okay.

1244
01:05:29,717 --> 01:05:31,469
‪Get up.

1245
01:05:33,429 --> 01:05:34,597
‪Go on.

1246
01:05:36,349 --> 01:05:37,350
‪Bye.

1247
01:05:37,433 --> 01:05:38,351
‪The sun's up.

1248
01:05:39,018 --> 01:05:39,852
‪That's how…

1249
01:05:40,811 --> 01:05:42,104
‪we stayed up the whole night.

1250
01:05:42,855 --> 01:05:46,025
‪We knew we liked each other

1251
01:05:46,108 --> 01:05:49,862
‪when we were talking this time,

1252
01:05:49,946 --> 01:05:50,988
‪so I had butterflies.

1253
01:05:52,490 --> 01:05:53,991
‪It was fun and exciting.

1254
01:05:55,242 --> 01:05:56,994
‪We talked a lot.

1255
01:05:57,078 --> 01:06:00,873
‪We joked around a lot
‪and talked about some serious stuff.

1256
01:06:00,957 --> 01:06:03,209
‪It was very memorable.

1257
01:06:06,963 --> 01:06:09,924
‪FINAL CHOICE D-DAY

1258
01:06:12,760 --> 01:06:15,721
‪JUNG-MIN PUTS ON MAKEUP BY HIMSELF

1259
01:06:16,847 --> 01:06:17,974
‪Is Ga-yeon awake?

1260
01:06:18,057 --> 01:06:18,975
‪She didn't sleep.

1261
01:06:24,271 --> 01:06:25,231
‪SNEAKS A PEEK

1262
01:06:26,857 --> 01:06:29,026
‪THEY DON'T EVEN GREET EACH OTHER

1263
01:06:46,252 --> 01:06:49,005
‪JUNG-MIN COMES LOOKING FOR GA-YEON

1264
01:06:49,588 --> 01:06:50,840
‪Can you do my makeup one last time?

1265
01:06:50,923 --> 01:06:52,174
‪One last makeup session?

1266
01:06:54,051 --> 01:06:55,970
‪He didn't say a word to her
‪until just now.

1267
01:06:56,053 --> 01:07:00,474
‪It's the same as when Ye-rim said,
‪"Let's be friends."

1268
01:07:00,558 --> 01:07:02,435
‪-It's the same thing.
‪-He's doing the same thing.

1269
01:07:03,686 --> 01:07:05,646
‪-A bit later.
‪-Your last makeup session.

1270
01:07:14,238 --> 01:07:15,573
‪Did you drink a lot?

1271
01:07:16,657 --> 01:07:18,242
‪I'm hungover for the first time.

1272
01:07:18,325 --> 01:07:19,702
‪How much did you drink?

1273
01:07:20,453 --> 01:07:23,122
‪I'm not sure. Maybe four or five bottles.

1274
01:07:23,205 --> 01:07:24,123
‪By yourself?

1275
01:07:25,708 --> 01:07:26,584
‪With others.

1276
01:07:31,380 --> 01:07:33,132
‪-All done.
‪-Good.

1277
01:07:36,093 --> 01:07:37,386
‪-Thanks.
‪-Mhm.

1278
01:07:41,557 --> 01:07:42,641
<i>‪It's here.</i>

1279
01:07:42,725 --> 01:07:44,643
‪-What is it?
‪-What came?

1280
01:07:45,227 --> 01:07:46,854
‪"It's the day of the final decision."

1281
01:07:46,937 --> 01:07:48,731
‪"Confess how you feel."

1282
01:07:49,273 --> 01:07:51,942
<i>‪The Final Stage</i>
<i>‪of the King of Hearts game.</i>

1283
01:07:52,526 --> 01:07:54,695
<i>‪The final choice vote will begin.</i>

1284
01:07:54,779 --> 01:07:56,655
‪I had to come in first no matter what.

1285
01:07:56,739 --> 01:07:57,782
‪I try not to lose.

1286
01:07:57,865 --> 01:07:59,992
‪I always tried to win.

1287
01:08:00,076 --> 01:08:01,911
‪I'm going to make him mine.

1288
01:08:01,994 --> 01:08:03,412
‪I won her over in the end.

1289
01:08:03,496 --> 01:08:05,206
‪Why should I be the one to give her up?

1290
01:08:05,289 --> 01:08:07,500
‪She's not an object,
‪but it's better if she's mine.

1291
01:08:07,583 --> 01:08:10,878
<i>‪Our subjects always get what they want,</i>

1292
01:08:10,961 --> 01:08:12,963
<i>‪but did they find</i>
<i>‪the love they were after?</i>

1293
01:08:28,187 --> 01:08:31,148
<i>‪Participants who used up</i>
<i>‪all your Heart Chips,</i>

1294
01:08:31,232 --> 01:08:33,734
<i>‪please call out the name</i>
<i>‪of the person you want to confess to</i>

1295
01:08:34,610 --> 01:08:36,487
<i>‪and confess your feelings.</i>

1296
01:08:38,364 --> 01:08:39,782
<i>‪Jung Hye-won.</i>

1297
01:08:39,865 --> 01:08:43,494
<i>‪Bring your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪and stand in front of the table.</i>

1298
01:08:51,001 --> 01:08:52,044
‪I want

1299
01:08:52,920 --> 01:08:56,257
‪to confess my feelings
‪to Jung Ha-yoon

1300
01:08:56,841 --> 01:08:58,926
‪and give him my heart.

1301
01:08:59,009 --> 01:09:01,387
‪HYE-WON → HA-YOON
‪FINAL CHOICE

1302
01:09:01,720 --> 01:09:03,639
‪YESTERDAY NIGHT, FINAL HEART CHIP VOTE

1303
01:09:04,223 --> 01:09:07,101
<i>‪I spent all my Heart Chips on Ha-yoon.</i>

1304
01:09:07,184 --> 01:09:09,812
‪JUNG HYE-WON COMPLETED VOTING
‪ALL HEART CHIPS → HA-YOON

1305
01:09:11,480 --> 01:09:13,482
<i>‪Ha-yoon's groundedness</i>

1306
01:09:14,191 --> 01:09:16,819
<i>‪served as fresh motivation to me.</i>

1307
01:09:16,902 --> 01:09:18,362
<i>‪He didn't put pressure on me,</i>

1308
01:09:19,488 --> 01:09:22,324
<i>‪but approached me like a calm lake.</i>

1309
01:09:22,408 --> 01:09:23,450
‪Our queen.

1310
01:09:24,034 --> 01:09:24,994
‪Our secure participant.

1311
01:09:25,077 --> 01:09:28,455
‪But honestly, even putting his job aside,
‪I would pick Ha-yoon.

1312
01:09:37,840 --> 01:09:40,301
‪Ha-yoon.

1313
01:09:40,384 --> 01:09:44,471
‪I'm so grateful that you had the courage

1314
01:09:45,055 --> 01:09:47,308
‪to open up and share
‪your feelings with me.

1315
01:09:47,892 --> 01:09:49,977
‪Let's talk more in the real world.

1316
01:09:52,146 --> 01:09:55,482
<i>‪He's an invaluable person to me.</i>

1317
01:09:55,566 --> 01:09:59,486
‪Ha-yoon is such a great guy,

1318
01:09:59,570 --> 01:10:04,617
‪and I wondered if a guy like that
‪could handle someone like me.

1319
01:10:04,700 --> 01:10:08,579
‪Even I don't always know
‪where I'll pivot next.

1320
01:10:08,662 --> 01:10:12,291
<i>‪So could a reserved guy like Ha-yoon</i>

1321
01:10:12,374 --> 01:10:15,044
<i>‪understand a girl like me?</i>

1322
01:10:15,628 --> 01:10:18,380
<i>‪If you want to confess your feelings,</i>
<i>‪after you confess,</i>

1323
01:10:18,464 --> 01:10:21,091
<i>‪put all your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪into the glass jar.</i>

1324
01:10:21,175 --> 01:10:22,801
<i>‪If you wish to turn them down,</i>

1325
01:10:22,885 --> 01:10:25,596
<i>‪say your final goodbye</i>
<i>‪and return to your position.</i>

1326
01:10:30,267 --> 01:10:31,101
‪Hye-won.

1327
01:10:32,937 --> 01:10:35,522
‪You were my choice
‪from the beginning to the end.

1328
01:10:35,606 --> 01:10:38,567
‪Once we get out, let's eat a lot
‪of good food and talk for hours.

1329
01:10:39,693 --> 01:10:40,527
‪I'm thankful too.

1330
01:10:47,618 --> 01:10:50,120
‪JUNG HA-YOON COMPLETED VOTING
‪ALL CHIPS → JUNG HYE-WON

1331
01:10:50,913 --> 01:10:54,291
<i>‪Hye-won bounces around,</i>
<i>‪you never know where she'll go next.</i>

1332
01:10:54,833 --> 01:11:00,047
‪I find that side of her really adorable.

1333
01:11:01,298 --> 01:11:04,343
‪I think I can keep her centered

1334
01:11:04,426 --> 01:11:08,097
‪so she doesn't bounce too far
‪in any one direction.

1335
01:11:08,764 --> 01:11:10,849
<i>‪I'd like us to find that balance together.</i>

1336
01:11:11,558 --> 01:11:14,019
‪HA-YOON → HYE-WON
‪FINAL CHOICE

1337
01:11:17,731 --> 01:11:19,191
‪Wow, congratulations.

1338
01:11:19,275 --> 01:11:20,359
‪Congratulations.

1339
01:11:21,026 --> 01:11:22,486
<i>‪Congratulations.</i>

1340
01:11:22,569 --> 01:11:26,407
<i>‪You are the first couple</i>
<i>‪of the first King of Hearts Game.</i>

1341
01:11:28,284 --> 01:11:30,494
‪JUNG HYE-WON, JUNG HA-YOON

1342
01:11:30,577 --> 01:11:31,870
‪What now?

1343
01:11:35,708 --> 01:11:38,127
<i>‪Even if we didn't meet in here,</i>

1344
01:11:38,210 --> 01:11:41,547
‪if I had crossed her in the street
‪or met her randomly somewhere,

1345
01:11:41,630 --> 01:11:44,717
‪I'd still have found her attractive
‪and fallen for her.

1346
01:11:44,800 --> 01:11:48,262
‪We might go to a cafe.
‪Hye-won likes peppermint tea.

1347
01:11:48,345 --> 01:11:51,557
‪I can also enjoy tea together.
‪I think that's how we'll spend our time.

1348
01:11:51,640 --> 01:11:54,768
‪We'll have some more peppermint tea,

1349
01:11:54,852 --> 01:11:56,437
‪talk some more,

1350
01:11:56,520 --> 01:11:59,023
‪and see other sides of each other.

1351
01:12:04,361 --> 01:12:07,531
‪JUNG HA-YOON AND JUNG HYE-WON
‪FINAL COUPLE

1352
01:12:08,365 --> 01:12:10,034
<i>‪Moon Chae-rin.</i>

1353
01:12:10,117 --> 01:12:13,871
<i>‪Bring your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪and stand in front of the table.</i>

1354
01:12:19,084 --> 01:12:24,214
<i>‪I used all my remaining Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪on Park Do-geon.</i>

1355
01:12:24,298 --> 01:12:25,716
<i>‪I made him my final choice.</i>

1356
01:12:29,636 --> 01:12:32,806
‪MOON CHAE-RIN COMPLETED VOTING
‪ALL CHIPS → PARK DO-GEON

1357
01:12:34,141 --> 01:12:39,063
‪I want to give my heart to Park Do-geon.

1358
01:12:42,358 --> 01:12:45,152
‪CHAE-RIN → DO-GEON
‪FINAL CHOICE

1359
01:12:48,238 --> 01:12:51,075
<i>‪Honestly, when I found out</i>
<i>‪his age and profession,</i>

1360
01:12:51,158 --> 01:12:54,620
<i>‪I wasn't sure my feelings would grow.</i>

1361
01:12:54,703 --> 01:12:57,289
<i>‪I was a little worried.</i>

1362
01:12:57,373 --> 01:12:59,792
‪But even though I hesitated,

1363
01:12:59,875 --> 01:13:05,923
‪he wasn't discouraged
‪and kept making his feelings really clear.

1364
01:13:06,006 --> 01:13:09,885
<i>‪I think that's why my feelings</i>
<i>‪grew stronger rather than fade.</i>

1365
01:13:11,678 --> 01:13:12,930
‪Do-geon.

1366
01:13:14,556 --> 01:13:19,770
‪The moments we spent talking
‪and just being together

1367
01:13:20,521 --> 01:13:22,940
‪made me happy and excited.

1368
01:13:23,941 --> 01:13:24,942
‪Thank you for everything.

1369
01:13:26,443 --> 01:13:28,445
<i>‪My mind's made up.</i>

1370
01:13:28,529 --> 01:13:30,823
‪When I fall for someone,

1371
01:13:30,906 --> 01:13:34,326
<i>‪I only have eyes for them,</i>

1372
01:13:34,410 --> 01:13:36,453
<i>‪and Chae-rin's the one</i>
<i>‪who made me realize that.</i>

1373
01:13:38,122 --> 01:13:40,374
<i>‪We both expressed</i>
<i>‪our feelings to each other,</i>

1374
01:13:40,457 --> 01:13:42,835
<i>‪and I felt like we both</i>
<i>‪knew where we stood,</i>

1375
01:13:42,918 --> 01:13:46,839
<i>‪so I gave all my Heart Chips to Chae-rin.</i>

1376
01:13:49,007 --> 01:13:51,093
‪I've never been interested
‪in anyone else but you

1377
01:13:51,677 --> 01:13:53,637
‪from the start until now.

1378
01:13:55,305 --> 01:13:57,099
‪You said you wanted to go bowling.

1379
01:13:57,182 --> 01:13:58,684
‪Let's go bowling together.

1380
01:14:04,982 --> 01:14:07,401
‪DO-GEON → CHAE-RIN
‪FINAL CHOICE

1381
01:14:10,279 --> 01:14:13,824
‪Whenever Chae-rin's feeling down,
‪dance "like JENNIE" for her, Do-geon.

1382
01:14:13,907 --> 01:14:16,577
‪Yeah, dance at Gireum Station
‪so I can watch too.

1383
01:14:17,161 --> 01:14:18,078
<i>‪Congratulations.</i>

1384
01:14:18,162 --> 01:14:21,790
<i>‪You are the second couple</i>
<i>‪of the first King of Hearts game.</i>

1385
01:14:30,090 --> 01:14:31,800
<i>‪I'd just finished my military service</i>

1386
01:14:31,884 --> 01:14:34,678
‪when this great opportunity came along

1387
01:14:34,761 --> 01:14:37,806
‪and I got to meet Moon Chae-rin.

1388
01:14:37,890 --> 01:14:40,559
‪I feel very blessed.

1389
01:14:41,185 --> 01:14:43,395
‪I felt like his feelings for me

1390
01:14:44,646 --> 01:14:48,484
‪were just as strong as mine were for him.

1391
01:14:49,151 --> 01:14:51,278
‪I was really thankful for that.

1392
01:14:51,862 --> 01:14:58,327
<i>‪I hope we'll be just as excited</i>
<i>‪and comfortable even after we get out.</i>

1393
01:15:02,039 --> 01:15:04,958
‪DO-GEON AND CHAE-RIN
‪FINAL COUPLE

1394
01:15:05,042 --> 01:15:07,252
‪-They suit each other so well.
‪-They're a great match.

1395
01:15:07,336 --> 01:15:09,087
‪-How nice.
‪-Lovely.

1396
01:15:10,464 --> 01:15:12,341
<i>‪While I'm a little disappointed</i>‪…

1397
01:15:16,428 --> 01:15:20,807
<i>‪I feel like I did my best</i>
<i>‪in the time we were given,</i>

1398
01:15:21,642 --> 01:15:23,393
<i>‪so I don't think I have any regrets.</i>

1399
01:15:23,977 --> 01:15:26,980
‪YE-RIM'S FINAL MESSAGE TO KYUNG-HO

1400
01:15:27,814 --> 01:15:30,817
<i>‪I wrote, "I'm a better match</i>
<i>‪for you than Ga-yeon."</i>

1401
01:15:30,901 --> 01:15:32,194
‪I'M A BETTER MATCH FOR YOU THAN GA-YEON

1402
01:15:37,658 --> 01:15:39,743
‪It was the final chance we had

1403
01:15:41,036 --> 01:15:42,454
‪to confess our feelings

1404
01:15:42,538 --> 01:15:46,208
‪and the last chance
‪to express what's on our minds,

1405
01:15:46,291 --> 01:15:49,169
‪and I wanted to be
‪true to my feelings to the end.

1406
01:15:53,131 --> 01:15:55,133
‪YE-RIM USED ALL HER HEART CHIPS LAST NIGHT

1407
01:15:57,052 --> 01:15:59,388
‪LEE YE-RIM

1408
01:15:59,471 --> 01:16:01,890
‪She did her best. No regrets.

1409
01:16:01,974 --> 01:16:03,016
‪That's a good thing.

1410
01:16:03,100 --> 01:16:04,268
‪For sure.

1411
01:16:05,352 --> 01:16:06,395
<i>‪Lee Ye-rim.</i>

1412
01:16:06,937 --> 01:16:10,816
<i>‪Bring your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪and stand in front of the table.</i>

1413
01:16:17,573 --> 01:16:20,450
‪The person I want to give my heart

1414
01:16:20,534 --> 01:16:22,286
‪is Kang Kyung-ho.

1415
01:16:26,957 --> 01:16:29,626
‪YE-RIM → KYUNG-HO
‪FINAL CHOICE

1416
01:16:32,254 --> 01:16:34,131
<i>‪As soon as I saw him,</i>

1417
01:16:34,715 --> 01:16:36,925
<i>‪I thought he was my ideal type.</i>

1418
01:16:39,761 --> 01:16:41,263
<i>‪And then he came over,</i>

1419
01:16:41,930 --> 01:16:43,223
<i>‪sat next to me, held my hand,</i>

1420
01:16:43,307 --> 01:16:45,684
<i>‪and asked me out on a date.</i>

1421
01:16:45,767 --> 01:16:49,605
<i>‪It was such a thrill,</i>
<i>‪and a happy memory for me.</i>

1422
01:16:54,860 --> 01:16:55,694
‪I hope…

1423
01:16:58,071 --> 01:17:00,782
‪I'll be someone you remember.

1424
01:17:00,866 --> 01:17:04,202
‪Like you said, I'm a remarkable person,

1425
01:17:04,995 --> 01:17:06,079
‪so let's stay friends.

1426
01:17:10,876 --> 01:17:12,586
<i>‪If you wish to turn them down,</i>

1427
01:17:12,669 --> 01:17:15,422
<i>‪say your final goodbye</i>
<i>‪and return to your position.</i>

1428
01:17:16,131 --> 01:17:17,507
<i>‪If you want to confess your feelings,</i>

1429
01:17:17,591 --> 01:17:19,092
<i>‪after you confess,</i>

1430
01:17:19,176 --> 01:17:21,637
<i>‪put all your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪into the glass jar.</i>

1431
01:17:28,644 --> 01:17:30,646
‪You really are a remarkable person

1432
01:17:34,941 --> 01:17:37,277
‪and I don't think that will change.

1433
01:17:41,156 --> 01:17:42,449
‪Let's be friends.

1434
01:17:44,534 --> 01:17:45,577
‪What just happened?

1435
01:17:46,536 --> 01:17:47,579
‪Did he choke up?

1436
01:17:47,663 --> 01:17:48,872
<i>‪Let's be friends.</i>

1437
01:17:50,999 --> 01:17:52,793
‪-Did get tear up?
‪-His nose kind of…

1438
01:17:53,669 --> 01:17:54,961
‪Let's be friends.

1439
01:18:13,146 --> 01:18:17,442
<i>‪Kang Kyung-ho did not return</i>
<i>‪Lee Ye-rim's feelings.</i>

1440
01:18:18,026 --> 01:18:20,654
<i>‪Please put your glass jar</i>
<i>‪back in its original place</i>

1441
01:18:20,737 --> 01:18:22,489
<i>‪and return to your position.</i>

1442
01:18:31,957 --> 01:18:35,460
<i>‪Our timing was a bit off</i>

1443
01:18:35,544 --> 01:18:37,671
<i>‪and some other things didn't line up.</i>

1444
01:18:38,338 --> 01:18:40,507
‪I'm a bit disappointed about that.

1445
01:18:40,590 --> 01:18:42,300
‪But to be honest,

1446
01:18:42,384 --> 01:18:45,679
‪when all that stuff first went down,

1447
01:18:46,304 --> 01:18:47,973
‪I was a bit resentful

1448
01:18:48,056 --> 01:18:50,225
‪and obviously a little jealous.

1449
01:18:50,308 --> 01:18:53,395
‪I got angry when I felt
‪like I wasn't being respected,

1450
01:18:53,478 --> 01:18:55,605
‪but I know not everything can go
‪the way I want.

1451
01:18:55,689 --> 01:19:00,444
‪I realize now that I need
‪to respect his choices.

1452
01:19:01,027 --> 01:19:05,365
‪I was able to understand better
‪the more we talked.

1453
01:19:05,449 --> 01:19:08,660
‪And I think I learned how

1454
01:19:08,744 --> 01:19:13,582
‪to speak more gently
‪and initiate conversation.

1455
01:19:15,208 --> 01:19:19,588
‪I'm thankful that he heard me out.

1456
01:19:20,630 --> 01:19:22,424
‪I think he's a remarkable guy too.

1457
01:19:23,675 --> 01:19:24,843
‪I wanted to tell him that.

1458
01:19:26,928 --> 01:19:30,766
‪-She's bound to meet a better person.
‪-For sure.

1459
01:19:37,397 --> 01:19:38,356
<i>‪Park Ga-yeon.</i>

1460
01:19:38,440 --> 01:19:41,860
<i>‪Bring your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪and stand in front of the table.</i>

1461
01:19:50,911 --> 01:19:53,622
<i>‪If you want to confess</i>
<i>‪your feelings to Park Ga-yeon,</i>

1462
01:19:53,705 --> 01:19:57,000
<i>‪bring your Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪and stand in front of the table.</i>

1463
01:19:57,584 --> 01:20:00,462
<i>‪When you gain something,</i>
<i>‪you lose something too.</i>

1464
01:20:00,545 --> 01:20:02,756
<i>‪I have mixed feelings.</i>

1465
01:20:09,679 --> 01:20:12,349
<i>‪I used all my Heart Chips on Ga-yeon.</i>

1466
01:20:12,432 --> 01:20:15,143
‪KANG KYUNG-HO COMPLETED VOTING
‪ALL CHIPS → PARK GA-YEON

1467
01:20:15,227 --> 01:20:19,105
‪She made me feel things
‪I never expected to feel.

1468
01:20:19,189 --> 01:20:21,858
‪I think that's why I chose her in the end.

1469
01:20:25,070 --> 01:20:27,239
‪KYUNG-HO → GA-YEON
‪FINAL CHOICE

1470
01:20:37,958 --> 01:20:40,418
‪JUNG-MIN → GA-YEON
‪FINAL CHOICE

1471
01:20:43,046 --> 01:20:45,006
<i>‪A lot changed yesterday,</i>

1472
01:20:45,090 --> 01:20:47,884
<i>‪and I wish we had more time</i>
<i>‪and things worked out differently.</i>

1473
01:20:49,845 --> 01:20:52,264
<i>‪But my feelings didn't change much.</i>

1474
01:20:55,433 --> 01:20:57,936
‪YOU MADE THIS EXPERIENCE MORE FUN FOR ME
‪BY MAKING ME FEEL AND THINK MANY THINGS

1475
01:20:58,019 --> 01:21:00,021
‪EVEN THOUGH IT TURNED OUT THIS WAY,
‪THANKS FOR THE LAST FIVE DAYS

1476
01:21:00,981 --> 01:21:02,774
<i>‪She's the person I spoke to the most</i>

1477
01:21:02,858 --> 01:21:05,986
<i>‪and the person I was most attracted to.</i>

1478
01:21:06,570 --> 01:21:08,446
<i>‪She was the prettiest in my eyes.</i>

1479
01:21:14,119 --> 01:21:16,496
‪JUNG-MIN USED
‪ALL HIS HEART CHIPS LAST NIGHT

1480
01:21:20,417 --> 01:21:21,376
‪Ga-yeon.

1481
01:21:22,210 --> 01:21:26,756
‪First of all, thanks for spending
‪most of the last five days with me.

1482
01:21:29,217 --> 01:21:32,137
<i>‪She was the most fun</i>
<i>‪and comfortable to be around.</i>

1483
01:21:32,721 --> 01:21:34,472
‪Will you go on a date with me tomorrow?

1484
01:21:34,556 --> 01:21:35,390
‪Yes.

1485
01:21:39,936 --> 01:21:42,898
‪It's because of Ga-yeon
‪that I was able to feel this way.

1486
01:21:42,981 --> 01:21:45,525
<i>‪She gave me something</i>
<i>‪to look forward to.</i>

1487
01:21:47,152 --> 01:21:48,320
‪Seven, six…

1488
01:21:51,156 --> 01:21:54,284
<i>‪The talks we had</i>
<i>‪and the things we did together</i>

1489
01:21:54,910 --> 01:21:57,037
<i>‪on our dates were so much fun.</i>

1490
01:21:57,621 --> 01:21:58,914
‪Five days is huge.

1491
01:21:58,997 --> 01:22:01,207
‪It's not like they went home
‪at the end of the day.

1492
01:22:01,291 --> 01:22:03,752
‪-They were constantly together.
‪-Five days the whole time.

1493
01:22:03,835 --> 01:22:05,545
‪Those two were basically inseparable

1494
01:22:05,629 --> 01:22:06,880
‪and even physical.

1495
01:22:08,006 --> 01:22:11,801
‪I'd like to keep spending
‪most of my time with you,

1496
01:22:13,470 --> 01:22:16,097
‪and I'll keep rooting for you.

1497
01:22:33,657 --> 01:22:35,533
<i>‪The more time passed,</i>

1498
01:22:35,617 --> 01:22:38,119
<i>‪I was able to see many sides of Ga-yeon.</i>

1499
01:22:43,541 --> 01:22:45,919
‪I know you really like to win,

1500
01:22:49,130 --> 01:22:52,467
‪so I appreciated it
‪when you said you lost to me.

1501
01:22:55,762 --> 01:23:00,058
‪I was glad to share
‪this experience with you.

1502
01:23:02,894 --> 01:23:05,021
‪Let's leave this place together.

1503
01:23:07,440 --> 01:23:10,568
<i>‪I felt a lot of emotions</i>
<i>‪that I'd forgotten how to feel.</i>

1504
01:23:11,152 --> 01:23:12,904
‪Like feeling excited

1505
01:23:12,988 --> 01:23:14,739
‪or jealous.

1506
01:23:14,823 --> 01:23:20,704
‪Because of her and the situation
‪being out of my control,

1507
01:23:20,787 --> 01:23:22,914
‪the feeling of my head about to burst…

1508
01:23:22,998 --> 01:23:28,545
‪It brought up emotions I'd forgotten.

1509
01:23:29,212 --> 01:23:31,381
‪I think that will really stay with me.

1510
01:23:40,515 --> 01:23:43,852
<i>‪Park Ga-yeon, please give your answer</i>

1511
01:23:43,935 --> 01:23:45,562
<i>‪to each person's confession</i>

1512
01:23:46,062 --> 01:23:49,024
<i>‪and pour all the Heart Chips</i>
<i>‪of the person you choose</i>

1513
01:23:49,107 --> 01:23:50,984
<i>‪into your glass jar.</i>

1514
01:23:56,781 --> 01:24:01,161
‪PARK GA-YEON USED
‪ALL HER HEART CHIPS LAST NIGHT

1515
01:24:03,038 --> 01:24:03,913
‪Jung-min.

1516
01:24:06,833 --> 01:24:09,961
‪You're a really caring
‪and attentive person.

1517
01:24:10,545 --> 01:24:11,463
‪I will

1518
01:24:12,213 --> 01:24:14,132
‪keep rooting for you too.

1519
01:24:17,552 --> 01:24:19,471
‪Kyung-ho. You made

1520
01:24:20,889 --> 01:24:21,848
‪my heart race

1521
01:24:24,434 --> 01:24:25,477
‪and made me excited.

1522
01:24:27,979 --> 01:24:30,398
‪Let's take things calmly
‪and see each other for a long time.

1523
01:24:42,452 --> 01:24:45,080
‪GA-YEON → KYUNG-HO
‪FINAL CHOICE

1524
01:24:50,960 --> 01:24:54,631
<i>‪Park Ga-yeon did not return</i>
<i>‪Park Jung-min's feelings.</i>

1525
01:24:55,340 --> 01:24:57,801
<i>‪Please put your glass jar</i>
<i>‪back in its original place</i>

1526
01:24:57,884 --> 01:24:59,928
<i>‪and return to your position.</i>

1527
01:25:04,849 --> 01:25:06,559
<i>‪For me, the final choice means</i>

1528
01:25:07,310 --> 01:25:11,147
<i>‪choosing someone I could consider</i>
<i>‪having a serious relationship with.</i>

1529
01:25:11,231 --> 01:25:12,440
<i>‪That was Ga-yeon.</i>

1530
01:25:14,776 --> 01:25:17,403
‪It felt like I missed out
‪on something that's even rarer,

1531
01:25:17,487 --> 01:25:19,614
‪so it's that much more
‪sad and disappointing.

1532
01:25:22,659 --> 01:25:25,620
‪I feel like crying right now, honestly.

1533
01:25:27,122 --> 01:25:29,040
‪But I'll be okay when I get home.

1534
01:25:30,250 --> 01:25:31,501
‪Time heals all wounds.

1535
01:25:37,257 --> 01:25:39,467
‪I think Jung-min gave his all.

1536
01:25:39,551 --> 01:25:40,593
‪Of course,

1537
01:25:40,677 --> 01:25:43,054
‪I'd like to stay really good friends
‪once we get out.

1538
01:25:43,138 --> 01:25:46,516
‪But that might be asking for too much.

1539
01:25:46,599 --> 01:25:50,895
‪So however he feels
‪and whatever he decides to do,

1540
01:25:50,979 --> 01:25:52,814
‪I just have to accept it.

1541
01:25:53,773 --> 01:25:56,359
‪Kyung-ho confessed his feelings
‪and held hands with her too,

1542
01:25:56,442 --> 01:25:57,819
‪but they're not officially dating.

1543
01:25:58,862 --> 01:26:01,030
‪So who knows what could happen?

1544
01:26:01,739 --> 01:26:04,033
‪I took a ton of selfies with her
‪in matching outfits.

1545
01:26:04,617 --> 01:26:06,870
‪I won't delete them
‪even if she dates Kyung-ho.

1546
01:26:11,791 --> 01:26:12,959
<i>‪Congratulations.</i>

1547
01:26:13,042 --> 01:26:16,838
<i>‪You are the third couple</i>
<i>‪of the first King of Hearts game.</i>

1548
01:26:19,549 --> 01:26:21,843
‪PARK GA-YEON, KANG KYUNG-HO

1549
01:26:25,305 --> 01:26:26,890
<i>‪He's a charming guy.</i>

1550
01:26:27,473 --> 01:26:31,811
<i>‪He completely shattered</i>
<i>‪my idea of what I was looking for.</i>

1551
01:26:33,313 --> 01:26:36,357
‪It wasn't a matter of what my ideals were.

1552
01:26:36,441 --> 01:26:39,861
‪Kyung-ho was the person I felt drawn to.

1553
01:26:40,486 --> 01:26:42,864
‪And I know for sure I want to date him.

1554
01:26:43,323 --> 01:26:45,742
‪GA-YEON'S MESSAGE TO KYUNG-HO LAST NIGHT

1555
01:26:45,825 --> 01:26:48,745
<i>‪Let's take things calmly</i>
<i>‪and see other for a long time.</i>

1556
01:26:48,828 --> 01:26:51,456
<i>‪Let's meet up often</i>
<i>‪even after we get out.</i>

1557
01:26:51,831 --> 01:26:54,542
‪KYUNG-HO WROTE A SIMILAR MESSAGE

1558
01:26:55,585 --> 01:26:58,379
<i>‪I plan to see her for a long time,</i>

1559
01:26:58,463 --> 01:27:02,050
<i>‪but I want her to know</i>
<i>‪I have no intention of keeping it calm.</i>

1560
01:27:03,301 --> 01:27:06,012
<i>‪I hope we'll feel this way</i>

1561
01:27:06,930 --> 01:27:08,848
<i>‪and stay this way for a long time.</i>

1562
01:27:09,432 --> 01:27:12,435
‪KYUNG-HO AND GA-YEON
‪FINAL COUPLE

1563
01:27:21,945 --> 01:27:24,989
<i>‪The first King of Hearts game has ended.</i>

1564
01:27:30,870 --> 01:27:32,789
‪It's been a long road. Goodness.

1565
01:27:32,872 --> 01:27:33,831
‪Seriously.

1566
01:27:34,332 --> 01:27:35,875
‪Three couples. That's impressive.

1567
01:27:35,959 --> 01:27:37,335
‪There were three successful couples.

1568
01:27:37,418 --> 01:27:40,672
‪It could have been four couples
‪if not for that final twist at the end.

1569
01:27:40,755 --> 01:27:42,006
‪That's really impressive.

1570
01:27:43,007 --> 01:27:46,094
‪At first, the concept of a king
‪seemed kind of silly,

1571
01:27:46,177 --> 01:27:47,887
<i>‪and I wondered if we even needed it.</i>

1572
01:27:49,222 --> 01:27:52,058
‪But the king became
‪increasingly important.

1573
01:27:52,141 --> 01:27:56,646
‪The people who weren't king
‪became more dependent on the king.

1574
01:27:57,814 --> 01:28:01,109
<i>‪So the king's choices</i>
<i>‪and one's relationship with the king</i>

1575
01:28:01,192 --> 01:28:02,986
<i>‪became really important.</i>

1576
01:28:03,486 --> 01:28:06,781
‪It was a really weird
‪dating show in that way.

1577
01:28:06,864 --> 01:28:09,158
‪When you wanted to go
‪on a date with someone,

1578
01:28:09,242 --> 01:28:14,372
<i>‪you had to go to the king and say,</i>
<i>‪"I want to date this person,"</i>

1579
01:28:14,455 --> 01:28:17,917
‪so it made me a lot more proactive.

1580
01:28:18,001 --> 01:28:22,463
‪And it made me more aware of my feelings.

1581
01:28:22,547 --> 01:28:23,673
‪Make me king.

1582
01:28:23,756 --> 01:28:25,633
‪Either me or Ga-yeon
‪will become king today.

1583
01:28:25,717 --> 01:28:27,218
‪We have to keep her in check.

1584
01:28:27,302 --> 01:28:29,595
‪For the sake of love,

1585
01:28:29,679 --> 01:28:32,557
‪I came up with strategies
‪and plotted and schemed.

1586
01:28:32,640 --> 01:28:36,853
‪Have I always been the kind of person
‪who goes this far for love?

1587
01:28:36,936 --> 01:28:39,022
‪We can use underhanded tactics.

1588
01:28:39,105 --> 01:28:43,109
‪The only tactic I can use now
‪is making you king.

1589
01:28:43,192 --> 01:28:46,863
‪The king played a huge role
‪in every aspect.

1590
01:28:46,946 --> 01:28:49,699
<i>‪You had to be good to the king</i>

1591
01:28:49,782 --> 01:28:53,661
<i>‪to get what you wanted.</i>
<i>‪That's how the game worked.</i>

1592
01:28:55,496 --> 01:28:59,334
‪Whoever you tried to keep in check

1593
01:28:59,417 --> 01:29:02,295
‪was a pretty clear indicator

1594
01:29:02,378 --> 01:29:04,213
‪of who they wanted to date.

1595
01:29:04,297 --> 01:29:05,923
‪It was so much fun.

1596
01:29:06,007 --> 01:29:10,011
‪You could indirectly find out
‪what the other person was feeling,

1597
01:29:10,094 --> 01:29:11,554
‪so that was nice.

1598
01:29:11,637 --> 01:29:15,141
‪The King of Hearts Game
‪gave us a lot of chances.

1599
01:29:15,224 --> 01:29:18,061
‪On top of love,
‪there was more fun involved.

1600
01:29:19,479 --> 01:29:21,230
‪AND NOW

1601
01:29:21,814 --> 01:29:23,483
‪"And now…"

1602
01:29:23,566 --> 01:29:24,484
‪Here we go.

1603
01:29:24,567 --> 01:29:25,526
‪Will we see results?

1604
01:29:25,610 --> 01:29:27,278
‪-Of course, we will!
‪-We have to!

1605
01:29:27,362 --> 01:29:31,157
‪DO-GEON AND CHAE-RIN
‪MET IN HYEHWA THE VERY NEXT DAY

1606
01:29:32,492 --> 01:29:36,329
‪THEY WENT ON A BOWLING DATE AS PROMISED

1607
01:30:01,062 --> 01:30:04,440
‪GA-YEON & KYUNG-HO, HYE-WON & HA-YOON
‪WENT ON A DOUBLE DATE

1608
01:30:05,024 --> 01:30:06,943
‪They even went on a double date!

1609
01:30:08,194 --> 01:30:10,655
‪UNBOXING WHAT THEY MADE
‪DURING THE POTTERY DATE

1610
01:30:10,738 --> 01:30:12,281
‪Thanks.

1611
01:30:12,365 --> 01:30:13,908
‪-I'll use this well.
‪-Okay.

1612
01:30:13,991 --> 01:30:15,034
‪Bon app<b>‪é</b>‪tit.

1613
01:30:28,506 --> 01:30:30,675
‪A DAY OUT BY THE HANGANG RIVER

1614
01:30:30,758 --> 01:30:33,219
‪I prefer the 7 to the SE.

1615
01:30:33,302 --> 01:30:34,137
‪The color?

1616
01:30:34,220 --> 01:30:36,222
‪DRAWING TOGETHER

1617
01:30:36,305 --> 01:30:39,183
‪CUSTOM COUPLE CAPS

1618
01:30:39,267 --> 01:30:42,145
‪COUPLE CAP SELFIES

1619
01:30:49,235 --> 01:30:51,445
‪Like that, the King of Heart game

1620
01:30:52,280 --> 01:30:53,114
‪is over.

1621
01:30:53,197 --> 01:30:55,491
‪More importantly,
‪it's the end of The Love Lab.

1622
01:30:55,575 --> 01:30:56,742
‪That's right.

1623
01:30:56,826 --> 01:30:58,703
‪-It's a shame.
‪-What did you think of it?

1624
01:30:58,786 --> 01:31:00,246
‪It was so much fun.

1625
01:31:00,329 --> 01:31:03,374
‪-It was.
‪-Seriously, I just had fun watching.

1626
01:31:03,457 --> 01:31:04,292
‪Same.

1627
01:31:04,375 --> 01:31:08,045
‪The participants were all so sincere

1628
01:31:08,129 --> 01:31:09,839
‪and it was so much fun.

1629
01:31:09,922 --> 01:31:12,341
‪I would like to thank everyone.

1630
01:31:12,425 --> 01:31:14,177
‪We're sorry if you got hurt
‪by any of our reactions.

1631
01:31:14,260 --> 01:31:16,554
‪We were just being dramatic
‪to make some money.

1632
01:31:16,637 --> 01:31:19,891
‪If we can do so,
‪let's go for a meal together…

1633
01:31:19,974 --> 01:31:20,933
‪Come to our wrap-up dinner!

1634
01:31:21,017 --> 01:31:23,728
‪Come and tell us what was hard
‪and what was frustrating,

1635
01:31:23,811 --> 01:31:24,687
‪Ye-rim!

1636
01:31:25,188 --> 01:31:27,148
‪Let's all get together…

1637
01:31:27,231 --> 01:31:29,192
‪-And talk it all out.
‪-Yes, let's talk it all out!

1638
01:31:29,275 --> 01:31:30,526
‪-Yes.
‪-Yeah.

1639
01:31:30,610 --> 01:31:32,778
‪-Thank you.
‪-Thank you.

1640
01:31:42,872 --> 01:31:44,874
‪Subtitle translation by: Hannah Og Nam

1641
01:31:44,957 --> 01:31:47,752
‪THE LOVE LAB
